A||||5||PAUL88GT||Dash paint question||||5||
Z||000000||PAUL88GT||05-14-2001||03:22 PM||||I just painted the dash of my 86SE with SEM vinyl paint.  Brown on top and tan everywhere else.  I used the original color scheme. I removed the dash to paint it.  Should I put clear coat over the vinyl paint?  If so, how may coats and what brand of clear coat should I use?  TIA<P>Paul||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroLisa||05-14-2001||03:34 PM||||I know of no clear coat that is good over vinyl paint, and also don't think its necessary. If you prepped it well enough before painting, it should stick without a problem and not scratch off with normal use.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/biohazard_racing/lisaonhood.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||PAUL88GT||05-14-2001||03:39 PM||||Thanks Fierolisa.  I cleaned it good with acetone before painting.  I looks great.  It is just dull.  I will just put on Armour All in a few a days after I reinstall it to restore the shine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroLisa||05-14-2001||04:04 PM||||Be careful with armor all- I don't use it anymore... If you have to touch up anything (since things *do* chip easier with a painted interior) it will be a big pain once you re-coat it with armor all... lots of cleaning with acetone again to get it all off.<BR>What I did was use a semi-metallic gray interior paint so mine always looks shiny, but it also doesn't look stock. I do have a dull black in some places and your right it does need more shine, but oh well.||||reg||1
Z||000004||jch82||05-14-2001||04:37 PM||||SEM makes a clear coat for vinyl. My buddy has used it and it worked just fine. A lot shinier as well.<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||05-14-2001||05:09 PM||||Well Ill give my 2 cents...<P>I'm in the middle of a complete resto.. of my '85 interior. I'm using "Performance Choice" by Mid America Corvette. <A HREF="http://www.madvet.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.madvet.com/</A> <P>Step #1 Clean part's with soap & water.<P>Step #2 Spray on "Vinyl Prep" (for vinyl) or "Plastic Prep" (for plastic) to remove any hard to remove wax or silicone<P>Step #3 Spray on "Flexible Bonding Clear"<P>Step #4 Spray on "Color Top Coat"<P>Step #5 Finish up with "Color Coat Clear High Gloss"<P><BR>I went with this stuff because I figured, If its good enough to restore a Classic Vette, Its good enough for a Fiero.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">       </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><I>If you want to add your Fiero to the collection, post or send me a photo. (Sent photos ONLY to: purplehazeracing@yahoo.com )</I><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 05-14-2001).]||||reg||14
